/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · 1 Chronicles chapters 11-15
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("1chronicles", [
{n:11, name:"David Crowned, Zion Taken", seal:{ref:"1 Chronicles 11:9",verse:"So David waxed greater and greater: for the LORD of hosts was with him."}, facts:["Did you know Jashobeam lifted his spear against three hundred men slain at one time, and David called these warriors men who strengthened themselves with him to make him king (1 Chronicles 11:10-11)?","Did you know David poured out the Bethlehem water as an offering to the LORD, calling it the blood of men who had put their lives in jeopardy to fetch it (1 Chronicles 11:18-19)?","Did you know Benaiah once slew a lion in a pit on a snowy day, and later faced a five-cubit Egyptian with only a staff, plucked the spear from the giant's hand, and slew him with it (1 Chronicles 11:22-23)?"], questions:[
{q:"Where did all Israel gather to make David king?", options:["Unto Hebron","Unto Gilgal","Unto Bethel","Unto Shiloh"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:1",verse:"Then all Israel gathered themselves to David unto Hebron, saying, Behold, we are thy bone and thy flesh.", insight:"They came to Hebron with one voice; unity gathers where God has spoken."},
{q:"What did the people remind David he had done in the days of Saul?", options:["He had led out and brought in Israel","He had built the walls of Hebron","He had slain Goliath at Elah","He had played the harp for Saul"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:2",verse:"And moreover in time past, even when Saul was king, thou wast he that leddest out and broughtest in Israel: and the LORD thy God said unto thee, Thou shalt feed my people Israel, and thou shalt be ruler over my people Israel, and thou shalt be ruler over my people Israel.", insight:"They remembered his leading before his crown; faithful service is the resume God reads."},
{q:"Before whom did David make covenant with the elders of Israel?", options:["Before the LORD","Before the ark of God","Before the tomb of Samuel","Before the men of war"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:3",verse:"Therefore came all the elders of Israel to the king to Hebron; and David made a covenant with them in Hebron before the LORD; and they anointed David king over Israel, according to the word of the LORD by Samuel.", insight:"Covenant before the LORD, not before men; promises kept in God's sight outlast politics."},
{q:"According to what word was David anointed king over Israel?", options:["The word of the LORD by Samuel","The word of the house of Saul","The decree of the elders","The lot of the priests"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:3",verse:"Therefore came all the elders of Israel to the king to Hebron; and David made a covenant with them in Hebron before the LORD; and they anointed David king over Israel, according to the word of the LORD by Samuel.", insight:"Anointed by God's word through Samuel; his kingship rested on promise, not on power."},
{q:"What did the Jebusites say when David came to Jerusalem?", options:["Thou shalt not come hither","We surrender the gates to thee","Take our king as thy servant","The LORD has given us into thy hand"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:5",verse:"And the inhabitants of Jebus said to David, Thou shalt not come hither. Nevertheless David took the castle of Zion, which is the city of David.", insight:"Mockery at the gate; the louder the taunt, the greater the triumph God is preparing."},
{q:"What reward did David promise to whoever smote the Jebusites first?", options:["Chief and captain","Half the kingdom","A thousand shekels of gold","The high priesthood"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:6",verse:"And David said, Whosoever smiteth the Jebusites first shall be chief and captain. So Joab the son of Zeruiah went first up, and was chief.", insight:"David rewarded courage with command; honor follows those who climb first for God's people."},
{q:"Who went up first against the Jebusites?", options:["Joab the son of Zeruiah","Abishai the son of Zeruiah","Jashobeam the Hachmonite","Benaiah the son of Jehoiada"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:6",verse:"And David said, Whosoever smiteth the Jebusites first shall be chief and captain. So Joab the son of Zeruiah went first up, and was chief.", insight:"Joab's daring won him command; zeal opens doors, though character must keep them."},
{q:"Why did David wax greater and greater?", options:["For the LORD of hosts was with him","For he married into many houses","For he stored up great riches","For the Philistines made peace with him"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:9",verse:"So David waxed greater and greater: for the LORD of hosts was with him.", insight:"Greatness is a byproduct of presence; the LORD of hosts with him was David's whole secret."},
{q:"How many did Jashobeam slay with his spear at one time?", options:["Three hundred","Eight hundred","One hundred","One thousand"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:11",verse:"And this is the number of the mighty men whom David had; Jashobeam, an Hachmonite, the chief of the captains: he lifted up his spear against three hundred slain by him at one time.", insight:"One man, one spear, three hundred; God multiplies the strength of the surrendered."},
{q:"Who was the chief of the captains among David's mighty men?", options:["Jashobeam, an Hachmonite","Eleazar the son of Dodo","Abishai the brother of Joab","Uriah the Hittite"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:11",verse:"And this is the number of the mighty men whom David had; Jashobeam, an Hachmonite, the chief of the captains: he lifted up his spear against three hundred slain by him at one time.", insight:"Jashobeam leads the roll of honor; God keeps a list of the faithful, and He knows the first name."},
{q:"What crop filled the parcel of ground at Pas-dammim where the Philistines gathered?", options:["Barley","Wheat","Flax","Lentils"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:13",verse:"He was with David at Pas-dammim, and there the Philistines were gathered together to battle, where was a parcel of ground full of barley; and the people fled from before the Philistines.", insight:"A barley field became a battlefield; God fights for ordinary ground, not only holy ground."},
{q:"What did David's men do in the midst of the barley field at Pas-dammim?", options:["They set themselves in the midst, delivered it, and slew the Philistines","They burned the field to deny it to the enemy","They hid themselves in the standing grain","They fled to the cave of Adullam"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:14",verse:"And they set themselves in the midst of that parcel, and delivered it, and slew the Philistines; and the LORD saved them by a great deliverance.", insight:"They stood in the middle of the field; sometimes faithfulness is simply refusing to run."},
{q:"Into what cave did three of the thirty captains come down to David?", options:["The cave of Adullam","The cave of Engedi","The cave of Makkedah","The cave of Machpelah"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:15",verse:"Now three of the thirty captains went down to the rock to David, into the cave of Adullam; and the host of the Philistines encamped in the valley of Rephaim.", insight:"Adullam, the cave of the outcast; God builds His kingdom with men the world threw away."},
{q:"For what water did David long while the Philistines held Bethlehem?", options:["The water of the well of Bethlehem at the gate","The pool of Hebron","The brook Kidron","The waters of Jericho"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:17",verse:"And David longed, and said, Oh that one would give me drink of the water of the well of Bethlehem, that is at the gate!", insight:"He longed for home's water in a foreign war; holy longing remembers where you belong."},
{q:"What did David do with the water the three mighty men brought him?", options:["He poured it out to the LORD","He drank it with thanks","He shared it with his captains","He stored it in his tent"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:18",verse:"And the three brake through the host of the Philistines, and drew water out of the well of Bethlehem, that was by the gate, and took it, and brought it to David: but David would not drink of it, but poured it out to the LORD,", insight:"He poured it out to the LORD; some gifts are too costly to keep, so offer them up."},
{q:"Why would David not drink the water?", options:["It was brought at the jeopardy of their lives","It was drawn from a defiled well","He had sworn a fast until evening","The Philistines had poisoned it"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:19",verse:"And said, My God forbid it me, that I should do this thing: shall I drink the blood of these men that have put their lives in jeopardy? for with the jeopardy of their lives they brought it. Therefore he would not drink it. These things did these three mightiest.", insight:"Shall I drink the blood of these men? He honored their risk more than his thirst; leaders count the cost others paid."},
{q:"Who was chief of the three mighty men?", options:["Abishai the brother of Joab","Jashobeam the Hachmonite","Eleazar the son of Dodo","Benaiah the son of Jehoiada"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:20",verse:"And Abishai the brother of Joab, he was chief of the three: for lifting up his spear against three hundred, he slew them, and had a name among the three.", insight:"Abishai, Joab's brother, chief of the three; courage ran in that family, for good and for ill."},
{q:"What rank did Abishai not attain, though he was more honourable than the two?", options:["He attained not to the first three","He attained not to the thirty","He attained not to the captains","He attained not to the guard"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:21",verse:"Of the three, he was more honourable than the two; for he was their captain: howbeit he attained not to the first three.", insight:"Second place, honored; God gives every man his measure, and contentment is part of courage."},
{q:"What did Benaiah slay in a pit on a snowy day?", options:["A lion","A bear","A leopard","A wolf"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:22",verse:"Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, the son of a valiant man of Kabzeel, who had done many acts; he slew two lionlike men of Moab: also he went down and slew a lion in a pit in a snowy day.", insight:"A lion in a pit on a snowy day; brave men do hard things in the worst weather."},
{q:"What did Benaiah do with the spear of the Egyptian who was five cubits high?", options:["He plucked it out of the Egyptian's hand, and slew him with it","He broke it over his knee","He threw it into the river","He carried it back to David as a trophy"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 11:23",verse:"And he slew an Egyptian, a man of great stature, five cubits high; and in the Egyptian’s hand was a spear like a weaver’s beam; and he went down to him with a staff, and plucked the spear out of the Egyptian’s hand, and slew him with his own spear.", insight:"He turned the giant's own weapon against him; God delights to win with the weaker hand."}
]},
{n:12, name:"The Host Gathers", seal:{ref:"1 Chronicles 12:22",verse:"For at that time day by day there came to David to help him, until it was a great host, like the host of God."}, facts:["Did you know the Gadites who joined David had faces like the faces of lions and were as swift as the roes upon the mountains, and they crossed the Jordan at flood stage in the first month (1 Chronicles 12:8, 12:15)?","Did you know the men of Issachar are remembered not for their swords but for having understanding of the times, to know what Israel ought to do (1 Chronicles 12:32)?","Did you know Zebulun sent fifty thousand men who could keep rank and were not of double heart, and from beyond the Jordan came one hundred and twenty thousand more (1 Chronicles 12:33, 12:37)?"], questions:[
{q:"To what place did the mighty men come to David while he kept himself close from Saul?", options:["To Ziklag","To Hebron","To the cave of Adullam","To the wilderness of Maon"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:1",verse:"Now these are they that came to David to Ziklag, while he yet kept himself close because of Saul the son of Kish: and they were among the mighty men, helpers of the war.", insight:"Ziklag, the hiding place; God gathers an army around you even in exile."},
{q:"Whose brethren were the skilled bowmen who came to David at Ziklag?", options:["Saul's brethren of Benjamin","David's brethren of Judah","Jonathan's brethren of Gibeah","Abner's brethren of the army"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:2",verse:"They were armed with bows, and could use both the right hand and the left in hurling stones and shooting arrows out of a bow, even of Saul’s brethren of Benjamin.", insight:"Saul's own tribesmen left him for David; loyalty follows God's anointing, not bloodlines."},
{q:"What could these Benjamites do with either the right hand or the left?", options:["Hurl stones and shoot arrows from the bow","Wield the sword and the spear","Climb walls and swim rivers","Track lions and snare birds"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:2",verse:"They were armed with bows, and could use both the right hand and the left in hurling stones and shooting arrows out of a bow, even of Saul’s brethren of Benjamin.", insight:"Both hands skilled for war; train every strength you have, and God will use them all."},
{q:"How are the Gadite warriors described?", options:["Their faces were like the faces of lions, and they were as swift as roes upon the mountains","They were tall as cedars and strong as oxen","They wore brass and carried iron shields","They marched in silence and never slept"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:8",verse:"And of the Gadites there separated themselves unto David into the hold to the wilderness men of might, and men of war fit for the battle, that could handle shield and buckler, whose faces were like the faces of lions, and were as swift as the roes upon the mountains;", insight:"Lions' faces, roes' swiftness; God shapes His servants with both courage and speed."},
{q:"How many did the least and the greatest of the Gadite captains command?", options:["The least over a hundred, the greatest over a thousand","The least over ten, the greatest over a hundred","The least over fifty, the greatest over five hundred","The least over a thousand, the greatest over ten thousand"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:14",verse:"These were of the sons of Gad, captains of the host: one of the least was over an hundred, and the greatest over a thousand.", insight:"A hundred or a thousand, each commanded his share; faithfulness is measured by obedience, not by size."},
{q:"When did the Gadites cross the Jordan, which had overflown all its banks?", options:["In the first month","In the seventh month","At the feast of weeks","In the winter rains"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:15",verse:"These are they that went over Jordan in the first month, when it had overflown all his banks; and they put to flight all them of the valleys, both toward the east, and toward the west.", insight:"They crossed at flood stage; some callings require you to move when the river is highest."},
{q:"What did David say to the men of Benjamin and Judah who came to the hold?", options:["If ye be come peaceably to help me, mine heart shall be knit unto you","Swear to me by the LORD before ye enter","Lay down your weapons at the gate","Go back, for I need no more men"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:17",verse:"And David went out to meet them, and answered and said unto them, If ye be come peaceably unto me to help me, mine heart shall be knit unto you: but if ye be come to betray me to mine enemies, seeing there is no wrong in mine hands, the God of our fathers look thereon, and rebuke it.", insight:"Peaceably, or to betray? David tested their hearts; welcome is wide, but discernment is wise."},
{q:"What did Amasai declare when the Spirit came upon him?", options:["Thine are we, David, and on thy side, thou son of Jesse","The LORD is with thee, thou mighty man","We have seen thy God fight for thee","Blessed be the God of Israel forever"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:18",verse:"Then the spirit came upon Amasai, who was chief of the captains, and he said, Thine are we, David, and on thy side, thou son of Jesse: peace, peace be unto thee, and peace be to thine helpers; for thy God helpeth thee. Then David received them, and made them captains of the band.", insight:"Thine are we, David; when the Spirit moves, loyalty speaks plainly and peace follows."},
{q:"What did David do with the men after Amasai's words?", options:["He received them, and made them captains of the band","He sent them back to Benjamin","He set them to guard the baggage","He numbered them among the porters"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:18",verse:"Then the spirit came upon Amasai, who was chief of the captains, and he said, Thine are we, David, and on thy side, thou son of Jesse: peace, peace be unto thee, and peace be to thine helpers; for thy God helpeth thee. Then David received them, and made them captains of the band.", insight:"He received them and gave them command; God turns yesterday's strangers into today's captains."},
{q:"Why did the Manassites not help David fight Saul with the Philistines?", options:["The lords of the Philistines sent him away, lest he turn to Saul","David refused their help out of pride","Saul had bribed them with silver","The ark forbade them to go"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:19",verse:"And there fell some of Manasseh to David, when he came with the Philistines against Saul to battle: but they helped them not: for the lords of the Philistines upon advisement sent him away, saying, He will fall to his master Saul to the jeopardy of our heads.", insight:"Sent away by suspicious lords; God sometimes closes a battle so you will fight His way."},
{q:"How many captains of the thousands of Manasseh fell to David as he went to Ziklag?", options:["Seven","Five","Ten","Twelve"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:20",verse:"As he went to Ziklag, there fell to him of Manasseh, Adnah, and Jozabad, and Jediael, and Michael, and Jozabad, and Elihu, and Zilthai, captains of the thousands that were of Manasseh.", insight:"Seven captains, named and counted; God knows the number of every quiet defection to His cause."},
{q:"How is the host that gathered day by day to David described?", options:["Like the host of God","Like the sand of the sea","Like the stars of the sky","Like a swarm of locusts"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:22",verse:"For at that time day by day there came to David to help him, until it was a great host, like the host of God.", insight:"Like the host of God; when God builds your army, heaven itself seems to muster."},
{q:"For what purpose did the armed bands come to David at Hebron?", options:["To turn the kingdom of Saul to him, according to the word of the LORD","To crown him king of Judah only","To avenge the death of Jonathan","To divide the spoil of the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:23",verse:"And these are the numbers of the bands that were ready armed to the war, and came to David to Hebron, to turn the kingdom of Saul to him, according to the word of the LORD.", insight:"To turn the kingdom, according to the word of the LORD; their mission was obedience to God's promise."},
{q:"How many of Judah that bare shield and spear came ready armed to the war?", options:["Six thousand and eight hundred","Seven thousand and one hundred","Four thousand and six hundred","Twenty thousand and eight hundred"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:24",verse:"The children of Judah that bare shield and spear were six thousand and eight hundred, ready armed to the war.", insight:"Six thousand eight hundred from his own tribe; start where you are, and God will add the rest."},
{q:"Why had only three thousand of Benjamin come to Hebron?", options:["The greatest part had kept the ward of the house of Saul","They were held back by famine","They feared the Philistines","They had not heard the call"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:29",verse:"And of the children of Benjamin, the kindred of Saul, three thousand: for hitherto the greatest part of them had kept the ward of the house of Saul.", insight:"Loyalty to Saul's house still held them; old allegiances die slowly, even after God has moved on."},
{q:"What gift made the men of Issachar famous?", options:["They had understanding of the times, to know what Israel ought to do","They could shoot with either hand","They were the swiftest runners in Israel","They sang the songs of the wars"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:32",verse:"And of the children of Issachar, which were men that had understanding of the times, to know what Israel ought to do; the heads of them were two hundred; and all their brethren were at their commandment.", insight:"Understanding of the times; the rarest strength in an army is knowing what the hour requires."},
{q:"How many heads of Issachar came to David?", options:["Two hundred","One hundred","Three hundred","Fifty"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:32",verse:"And of the children of Issachar, which were men that had understanding of the times, to know what Israel ought to do; the heads of them were two hundred; and all their brethren were at their commandment.", insight:"Two hundred heads, and all their brethren at their commandment; wise leadership multiplies loyalty."},
{q:"What is said of the fifty thousand of Zebulun?", options:["They could keep rank, and were not of double heart","They were the tallest men in Israel","They brought the most spoil","They feared no enemy by night"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:33",verse:"Of Zebulun, such as went forth to battle, expert in war, with all instruments of war, fifty thousand, which could keep rank: they were not of double heart.", insight:"Not of double heart; single-minded soldiers keep rank when others scatter."},
{q:"With what kind of heart did the men of war come to make David king?", options:["With a perfect heart","With a fearful heart","With a divided heart","With a proud heart"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:38",verse:"All these men of war, that could keep rank, came with a perfect heart to Hebron, to make David king over all Israel: and all the rest also of Israel were of one heart to make David king.", insight:"With a perfect heart; God crowns not only the king, but the wholehearted people behind him."},
{q:"What marked the great feast at Hebron when David was made king?", options:["There was joy in Israel, with bread, meat, figs, raisins, wine, and oil in abundance","They fasted three days in silence","They offered no sacrifice","The Philistines joined the feast"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 12:40",verse:"Moreover they that were nigh them, even unto Issachar and Zebulun and Naphtali, brought bread on asses, and on camels, and on mules, and on oxen, and meat, meal, cakes of figs, and bunches of raisins, and wine, and oil, and oxen, and sheep abundantly: for there was joy in Israel.", insight:"There was joy in Israel; God's appointments are worth celebrating with open hands and full tables."}
]},
{n:13, name:"The Ark and the Breach", seal:{ref:"1 Chronicles 13:3",verse:"And let us bring again the ark of our God to us: for we enquired not at it in the days of Saul."}, facts:["Did you know David's first attempt carried the ark in a new cart, but God had commanded it borne on the Levites' shoulders, a correction David himself later owned (1 Chronicles 13:7, 15:13)?","Did you know the place where Uzza died was called Perez-uzza, and it kept that name as a lasting warning about handling holy things (1 Chronicles 13:11)?","Did you know the ark spent three months in the house of Obed-edom the Gittite, and the LORD blessed his house and all that he had (1 Chronicles 13:13-14)?"], questions:[
{q:"With whom did David consult before fetching the ark?", options:["The captains of thousands and hundreds, and every leader","The priests and the prophets only","The elders of Judah alone","The messengers of the king of Tyre"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:1",verse:"And David consulted with the captains of thousands and hundreds, and with every leader.", insight:"He consulted before he acted; even a right desire deserves wise counsel first."},
{q:"Whom did David propose to gather from all the land of Israel?", options:["Their brethren everywhere, with the priests and Levites in their cities","The mighty men of war only","The singers and the porters","The sons of the prophets"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:2",verse:"And David said unto all the congregation of Israel, If it seem good unto you, and that it be of the LORD our God, let us send abroad unto our brethren every where, that are left in all the land of Israel, and with them also to the priests and Levites which are in their cities and suburbs, that they may gather themselves unto us:", insight:"All the brethren, priests and Levites too; the work of God belongs to the whole people, not a few."},
{q:"What neglect from the days of Saul did David name?", options:["We enquired not at the ark in the days of Saul","We offered no sacrifice in the days of Saul","We kept no passover in the days of Saul","We built no altar in the days of Saul"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:3",verse:"And let us bring again the ark of our God to us: for we enquired not at it in the days of Saul.", insight:"We enquired not at it; a generation can own the ark and never seek it. Do not repeat them."},
{q:"How did all the congregation answer David's proposal?", options:["The thing was right in the eyes of all the people","They feared to touch the ark","They asked for a sign from heaven","They appointed a committee"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:4",verse:"And all the congregation said that they would do so: for the thing was right in the eyes of all the people.", insight:"Right in the eyes of all the people; agreement is sweet, but it is no substitute for God's order."},
{q:"From where to where did David gather all Israel?", options:["From Shihor of Egypt even unto the entering of Hemath","From Dan even to Beersheba","From the Red Sea to the Euphrates","From Joppa to the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:5",verse:"So David gathered all Israel together, from Shihor of Egypt even unto the entering of Hemath, to bring the ark of God from Kirjath-jearim.", insight:"From border to border he summoned them; great undertakings deserve the whole nation's strength."},
{q:"What other name is given for Kirjath-jearim, where the ark was?", options:["Baalah","Kiriath-sepher","Beth-shemesh","Debir"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:6",verse:"And David went up, and all Israel, to Baalah, that is, to Kirjath-jearim, which belonged to Judah, to bring up thence the ark of God the LORD, that dwelleth between the cherubims, whose name is called on it.", insight:"Baalah, that is Kirjath-jearim; the ark had waited long in obscurity for its day of honor."},
{q:"How is the ark described as it rested at Kirjath-jearim?", options:["The ark of God the LORD, that dwelleth between the cherubims, whose name is called on it","The ark of the covenant, covered with pure gold","The ark of testimony, borne by the priests","The ark of the LORD, hidden from all men"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:6",verse:"And David went up, and all Israel, to Baalah, that is, to Kirjath-jearim, which belonged to Judah, to bring up thence the ark of God the LORD, that dwelleth between the cherubims, whose name is called on it.", insight:"He dwells between the cherubims; the God above the ark is nearer than the procession knew."},
{q:"How was the ark carried on its first journey toward Jerusalem?", options:["In a new cart","On the shoulders of the Levites","On the back of an ox","In the hands of the priests"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:7",verse:"And they carried the ark of God in a new cart out of the house of Abinadab: and Uzza and Ahio drave the cart.", insight:"A new cart, not consecrated shoulders; sincerity cannot sanctify a wrong method."},
{q:"Who drave the cart that carried the ark?", options:["Uzza and Ahio","Nadab and Abihu","Hophni and Phinehas","Eleazar and Ithamar"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:7",verse:"And they carried the ark of God in a new cart out of the house of Abinadab: and Uzza and Ahio drave the cart.", insight:"Uzza and Ahio drove it; good men can lead a holy thing the wrong way."},
{q:"How did David and all Israel celebrate before God?", options:["With all their might, and with singing","With solemn silence and fasting","With burnt offerings only","With weeping and lamentation"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:8",verse:"And David and all Israel played before God with all their might, and with singing, and with harps, and with psalteries, and with timbrels, and with cymbals, and with trumpets.", insight:"With all their might; joy before God is right, but joy must still walk in His order."},
{q:"With what instruments did they play before the ark?", options:["Harps, psalteries, timbrels, cymbals, and trumpets","Only the silver trumpets","Drums of war alone","The pipe and the viol"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:8",verse:"And David and all Israel played before God with all their might, and with singing, and with harps, and with psalteries, and with timbrels, and with cymbals, and with trumpets.", insight:"Every instrument sounding; heaven loves music, but music never excuses disobedience."},
{q:"At what place did Uzza put forth his hand to the ark?", options:["The threshingfloor of Chidon","The valley of Rephaim","The hill of Gibeon","The plain of Megiddo"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:9",verse:"And when they came unto the threshingfloor of Chidon, Uzza put forth his hand to hold the ark; for the oxen stumbled.", insight:"At Chidon's threshingfloor; judgment fell in an ordinary field, where nobody expected it."},
{q:"Why did Uzza put forth his hand to hold the ark?", options:["For the oxen stumbled","For the cart had broken","For the Philistines attacked","For the road was flooded"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:9",verse:"And when they came unto the threshingfloor of Chidon, Uzza put forth his hand to hold the ark; for the oxen stumbled.", insight:"The oxen stumbled; a reflex of the hand became a trespass of the heart. God means what He says about holiness."},
{q:"What happened to Uzza when he touched the ark?", options:["He died before God","He was struck blind","He was driven from the camp","He was made a leper"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:10",verse:"And the anger of the LORD was kindled against Uzza, and he smote him, because he put his hand to the ark: and there he died before God.", insight:"He died before God; the wages of irreverence are real, even when the motive looks kind."},
{q:"Why was the anger of the LORD kindled against Uzza?", options:["Because he put his hand to the ark","Because he drove the cart","Because he sang too loudly","Because he fled from the ark"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:10",verse:"And the anger of the LORD was kindled against Uzza, and he smote him, because he put his hand to the ark: and there he died before God.", insight:"Because he put his hand to it; God had forbidden what Uzza thought was help."},
{q:"What did David call the place where the breach was made?", options:["Perez-uzza","Baal-perazim","Ebenezer","Gilgal"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:11",verse:"And David was displeased, because the LORD had made a breach upon Uzza: wherefore that place is called Perez-uzza to this day.", insight:"Perez-uzza, the breach of Uzza; some places are named for warnings, not victories."},
{q:"How did David feel about the LORD's breach upon Uzza?", options:["He was displeased","He was indifferent","He was joyful","He was relieved"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:11",verse:"And David was displeased, because the LORD had made a breach upon Uzza: wherefore that place is called Perez-uzza to this day.", insight:"He was displeased; grief and confusion are honest, but they must still bow to God's holiness."},
{q:"What question did a frightened David ask that day?", options:["How shall I bring the ark of God home to me?","Where shall I flee from His presence?","Who will carry the ark for me?","Why has the LORD forsaken me?"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:12",verse:"And David was afraid of God that day, saying, How shall I bring the ark of God home to me?", insight:"How shall I bring it home? Fear asked the right question; reverence is the beginning of wisdom."},
{q:"Where did David leave the ark instead of bringing it to the city of David?", options:["In the house of Obed-edom the Gittite","In the house of Abinadab again","In the tabernacle at Gibeon","In the tent of the priests"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:13",verse:"So David brought not the ark home to himself to the city of David, but carried it aside into the house of Obed-edom the Gittite.", insight:"Aside into Obed-edom's house; sometimes God pauses our plans until we learn His way."},
{q:"How long did the ark remain with the family of Obed-edom?", options:["Three months","Forty days","One full year","Seven weeks"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 13:14",verse:"And the ark of God remained with the family of Obed-edom in his house three months. And the LORD blessed the house of Obed-edom, and all that he had.", insight:"Three months, and the LORD blessed his house; the presence that judges the careless blesses the reverent."}
]},
{n:14, name:"House and Victories", seal:{ref:"1 Chronicles 14:17",verse:"And the fame of David went out into all lands; and the LORD brought the fear of him upon all nations."}, facts:["Did you know Hiram king of Tyre, who sent cedar timber, masons and carpenters to build David's house, would later partner with David's son Solomon for the temple (1 Chronicles 14:1)?","Did you know David burned the Philistines' abandoned idols with fire instead of keeping them as trophies of war (1 Chronicles 14:12)?","Did you know God told David to wait for a sound of going in the tops of the mulberry trees, the signal that God Himself had gone before him into battle (1 Chronicles 14:15)?"], questions:[
{q:"Who sent messengers, cedar timber, masons and carpenters to David?", options:["Hiram king of Tyre","Pharaoh king of Egypt","The king of Moab","The elders of Gibeon"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:1",verse:"Now Hiram king of Tyre sent messengers to David, and timber of cedars, with masons and carpenters, to build him an house.", insight:"Hiram of Tyre built for David; God moves even foreign kings to honor His servant."},
{q:"For what purpose did Hiram send his workmen?", options:["To build David an house","To build a wall around Jerusalem","To raise a temple to the LORD","To dig wells in the Negeb"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:1",verse:"Now Hiram king of Tyre sent messengers to David, and timber of cedars, with masons and carpenters, to build him an house.", insight:"An house for the king; God gives His servants a settled place before He gives them settled rest."},
{q:"What did David perceive about his kingdom?", options:["The LORD had confirmed him king, and his kingdom was lifted up on high","His sons would reign forever without trouble","The Philistines would serve him as slaves","The ark would dwell in his house"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:2",verse:"And David perceived that the LORD had confirmed him king over Israel, for his kingdom was lifted up on high, because of his people Israel.", insight:"He perceived, not presumed; the wise king traces his rise to God's hand."},
{q:"What is recorded of David's family life at Jerusalem?", options:["He took more wives, and begat more sons and daughters","He lived alone in the castle","He sent his sons to Egypt","He married only Michal"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:3",verse:"And David took more wives at Jerusalem: and David begat more sons and daughters.", insight:"More wives, more children; increase is a blessing, but Scripture will show it also carried sorrow."},
{q:"Which four sons are named first among David's children born in Jerusalem?", options:["Shammua, Shobab, Nathan, and Solomon","Amnon, Chileab, Absalom, and Adonijah","Cain, Abel, Seth, and Enos","Reuben, Simeon, Levi, and Judah"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:4",verse:"Now these are the names of his children which he had in Jerusalem; Shammua, and Shobab, Nathan, and Solomon,", insight:"Shammua, Shobab, Nathan, Solomon; among these names stands the future temple builder."},
{q:"What did the Philistines do when they heard David was anointed king over all Israel?", options:["They went up to seek David","They sent him gifts of peace","They fled to the sea coast","They made a covenant with him"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:8",verse:"And when the Philistines heard that David was anointed king over all Israel, all the Philistines went up to seek David. And David heard of it, and went out against them.", insight:"They went up to seek him; new authority attracts old enemies. Expect the test after the anointing."},
{q:"What did David do when he heard the Philistines were coming?", options:["He went out against them","He hid in the cave of Adullam","He sent tribute to Gath","He fled to the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:8",verse:"And when the Philistines heard that David was anointed king over all Israel, all the Philistines went up to seek David. And David heard of it, and went out against them.", insight:"He went out against them; the anointed king did not wait for trouble to come to him."},
{q:"In what valley did the Philistines spread themselves?", options:["The valley of Rephaim","The valley of Elah","The valley of Achor","The valley of Sorek"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:9",verse:"And the Philistines came and spread themselves in the valley of Rephaim.", insight:"The valley of Rephaim, valley of giants; David faced the old battleground with a new crown."},
{q:"What two questions did David ask God before the battle?", options:["Shall I go up against the Philistines? And wilt thou deliver them into mine hand?","Shall I number the people? And wilt thou bless the harvest?","Shall I build Thee an house? And wilt thou dwell therein?","Shall I spare the captives? And wilt thou give me peace?"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:10",verse:"And David enquired of God, saying, Shall I go up against the Philistines? and wilt thou deliver them into mine hand? And the LORD said unto him, Go up; for I will deliver them into thine hand.", insight:"Shall I go? Wilt Thou deliver? Ask both the duty and the outcome before you march."},
{q:"What was God's answer to David?", options:["Go up; for I will deliver them into thine hand","Stay in the hold and wait","Send thy servants first","Make peace with the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:10",verse:"And David enquired of God, saying, Shall I go up against the Philistines? and wilt thou deliver them into mine hand? And the LORD said unto him, Go up; for I will deliver them into thine hand.", insight:"Go up, for I will deliver; when God gives both the command and the promise, obedience is safe."},
{q:"How did David describe God's victory at Baal-perazim?", options:["God hath broken in upon mine enemies by mine hand like the breaking forth of waters","The LORD hath thundered from heaven upon them","The mountains melted before His face","The earth opened and swallowed them"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:11",verse:"So they came up to Baal-perazim; and David smote them there. Then David said, God hath broken in upon mine enemies by mine hand like the breaking forth of waters: therefore they called the name of that place Baal-perazim.", insight:"Like the breaking forth of waters; God's victories come sudden, strong, and unstoppable."},
{q:"What was the place of victory called?", options:["Baal-perazim","Perez-uzza","Ebenezer","Baal-zephon"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:11",verse:"So they came up to Baal-perazim; and David smote them there. Then David said, God hath broken in upon mine enemies by mine hand like the breaking forth of waters: therefore they called the name of that place Baal-perazim.", insight:"Baal-perazim, the lord of breakings through; name your victories for what God did, not what you did."},
{q:"What did David do with the gods the Philistines left behind?", options:["He gave commandment, and they were burned with fire","He set them up as trophies in Jerusalem","He cast them into the sea","He sold them for silver"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:12",verse:"And when they had left their gods there, David gave a commandment, and they were burned with fire.", insight:"Burned with fire; idols deserve the flame, not a place in the museum."},
{q:"What did the Philistines do after their defeat?", options:["They yet again spread themselves abroad in the valley","They sued for peace","They returned to their own land","They joined themselves to David"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:13",verse:"And the Philistines yet again spread themselves abroad in the valley.", insight:"Yet again they spread; defeated enemies return, so pray and watch after every victory."},
{q:"What new orders did God give David for the second battle?", options:["Go not up after them; turn away, and come upon them over against the mulberry trees","Go up quickly before they escape","Wait seven days and fast","Divide thy army into three parts"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:14",verse:"Therefore David enquired again of God; and God said unto him, Go not up after them; turn away from them, and come upon them over against the mulberry trees.", insight:"Not the same way twice; God varies His methods so we keep listening instead of copying."},
{q:"What did David do before the second battle?", options:["He enquired again of God","He numbered his army","He offered a burnt offering","He consulted the captains"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:14",verse:"Therefore David enquired again of God; and God said unto him, Go not up after them; turn away from them, and come upon them over against the mulberry trees.", insight:"He enquired again; yesterday's victory is no excuse for today's presumption."},
{q:"What sign was David to wait for in the mulberry trees?", options:["A sound of going in the tops of the mulberry trees","A wind that shook the branches","A light upon the leaves","The singing of birds"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:15",verse:"And it shall be, when thou shalt hear a sound of going in the tops of the mulberry trees, that then thou shalt go out to battle: for God is gone forth before thee to smite the host of the Philistines.", insight:"A sound of going in the treetops; learn to hear heaven moving before you move."},
{q:"Why was the sound in the mulberry trees the signal to attack?", options:["For God is gone forth before thee to smite the host of the Philistines","For the Philistines were asleep","For the wind favored his archers","For his reinforcements had arrived"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:15",verse:"And it shall be, when thou shalt hear a sound of going in the tops of the mulberry trees, that then thou shalt go out to battle: for God is gone forth before thee to smite the host of the Philistines.", insight:"God gone forth before thee; the best battles are the ones heaven starts first."},
{q:"How far did David's men smite the Philistines?", options:["From Gibeon even to Gazer","From Hebron even to Beersheba","From Joppa even to Ekron","From Bethel even to Ai"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:16",verse:"David therefore did as God commanded him: and they smote the host of the Philistines from Gibeon even to Gazer.", insight:"From Gibeon to Gazer; obedience that follows God's signal reaps a full harvest."},
{q:"What did the LORD do after David's victories?", options:["He brought the fear of David upon all nations","He gave David rest from all enemies","He sent rain upon the land","He multiplied David's flocks"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 14:17",verse:"And the fame of David went out into all lands; and the LORD brought the fear of him upon all nations.", insight:"The fear of him upon all nations; God Himself advertises the victories He gives."}
]},
{n:15, name:"The Ark Comes Home", seal:{ref:"1 Chronicles 15:28",verse:"Thus all Israel brought up the ark of the covenant of the LORD with shouting, and with sound of the cornet, and with trumpets, and with cymbals, making a noise with psalteries and harps."}, facts:["Did you know David openly owned the first failure, saying 'we sought him not after the due order,' and this time the Levites bore the ark upon their shoulders with the staves (1 Chronicles 15:13, 15:15)?","Did you know the music was ordered by family: Heman, Asaph and Ethan on cymbals of brass, psalteries on Alamoth, harps on the Sheminith, with Chenaniah instructing the song because he was skilful (1 Chronicles 15:19-22)?","Did you know David danced in a robe of fine linen and an ephod of linen, and Michal the daughter of Saul despised him in her heart for it (1 Chronicles 15:27, 15:29)?"], questions:[
{q:"What preparations did David make for the ark in the city of David?", options:["He prepared a place for it, and pitched a tent for it","He built a temple of cedar for it","He dug a vault beneath the castle","He raised an altar of brass"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:1",verse:"And David made him houses in the city of David, and prepared a place for the ark of God, and pitched for it a tent.", insight:"A place prepared, a tent pitched; God honors the heart that gets ready before He comes."},
{q:"Who alone ought to carry the ark of God, according to David?", options:["The Levites","The priests only","The mighty men","The elders of Israel"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:2",verse:"Then David said, None ought to carry the ark of God but the Levites: for them hath the LORD chosen to carry the ark of God, and to minister unto him for ever.", insight:"None but the Levites; God's work has God's order, and the order is not optional."},
{q:"To what city did David gather all Israel to bring up the ark?", options:["To Jerusalem","To Hebron","To Shiloh","To Gibeon"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:3",verse:"And David gathered all Israel together to Jerusalem, to bring up the ark of the LORD unto his place, which he had prepared for it.", insight:"To Jerusalem; the ark was coming to the city God had chosen for His name."},
{q:"How many of the sons of Kohath, under Uriel the chief, were numbered?", options:["An hundred and twenty","Two hundred and twenty","An hundred and thirty","Fourscore"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:5",verse:"Of the sons of Kohath; Uriel the chief, and his brethren an hundred and twenty:", insight:"One hundred and twenty of Kohath; every family had its number, and every number its place."},
{q:"Which Levitical clan brought the most brethren, two hundred and twenty?", options:["The sons of Merari, under Asaiah","The sons of Kohath, under Uriel","The sons of Gershom, under Joel","The sons of Elizaphan, under Shemaiah"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:6",verse:"Of the sons of Merari; Asaiah the chief, and his brethren two hundred and twenty:", insight:"Two hundred and twenty of Merari; God counts the quiet carriers, not only the singers."},
{q:"Which two priests did David call for the bringing up of the ark?", options:["Zadok and Abiathar","Eleazar and Ithamar","Hilkiah and Azariah","Jehoiada and Zechariah"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:11",verse:"And David called for Zadok and Abiathar the priests, and for the Levites, for Uriel, Asaiah, and Joel, Shemaiah, and Eliel, and Amminadab,", insight:"Zadok and Abiathar; leadership in worship must be called, not assumed."},
{q:"What did David command the chief of the fathers of the Levites to do?", options:["Sanctify yourselves, both ye and your brethren","Wash your garments in the brook","Bring offerings of gold","Number all the people"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:12",verse:"And said unto them, Ye are the chief of the fathers of the Levites: sanctify yourselves, both ye and your brethren, that ye may bring up the ark of the LORD God of Israel unto the place that I have prepared for it.", insight:"Sanctify yourselves; those who carry holy things must first be made holy."},
{q:"Why, said David, had the LORD made a breach upon them at the first?", options:["For that we sought him not after the due order","For that we sang without the Levites","For that we brought too few sacrifices","For that we consulted not the priests"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:13",verse:"For because ye did it not at the first, the LORD our God made a breach upon us, for that we sought him not after the due order.", insight:"Not after the due order; David named the failure plainly. Confession is the road back to blessing."},
{q:"How was the ark now carried up to Jerusalem?", options:["Upon the shoulders of the Levites, with the staves thereon","In a new cart drawn by oxen","In the hands of the captains","Upon the back of a mule"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:15",verse:"And the children of the Levites bare the ark of God upon their shoulders with the staves thereon, as Moses commanded according to the word of the LORD.", insight:"On shoulders, with the staves; obedience done God's way carries what carts cannot."},
{q:"What instruments did the appointed singers use?", options:["Psalteries and harps and cymbals","Trumpets and cornets only","The timbrel and the pipe","The viol and the organ"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:16",verse:"And David spake to the chief of the Levites to appoint their brethren to be the singers with instruments of musick, psalteries and harps and cymbals, sounding, by lifting up the voice with joy.", insight:"Psalteries, harps, cymbals; God gave music many voices so joy could sound in full."},
{q:"Who were the three chief singers appointed by the Levites?", options:["Heman, Asaph, and Ethan","Chenaniah, Berechiah, and Elkanah","Zechariah, Jaaziel, and Shemiramoth","Uriel, Asaiah, and Joel"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:17",verse:"So the Levites appointed Heman the son of Joel; and of his brethren, Asaph the son of Berechiah; and of the sons of Merari their brethren, Ethan the son of Kushaiah;", insight:"Heman, Asaph, Ethan; named and appointed, for God uses known servants in ordered service."},
{q:"With what did Heman, Asaph, and Ethan sound?", options:["With cymbals of brass","With trumpets of silver","With harps of gold","With cornets of ram's horn"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:19",verse:"So the singers, Heman, Asaph, and Ethan, were appointed to sound with cymbals of brass;", insight:"Cymbals of brass; even the loudest praise is ordered praise when God appoints it."},
{q:"Which instruments played with harps on the Sheminith to excel?", options:["The harps themselves, with Mattithiah, Elipheleh, Mikneiah, Obed-edom, Jeiel, and Azaziah","The psalteries on Alamoth","The trumpets of the priests","The timbrels of the dancers"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:21",verse:"And Mattithiah, and Elipheleh, and Mikneiah, and Obed-edom, and Jeiel, and Azaziah, with harps on the Sheminith to excel.", insight:"Harps on the Sheminith to excel; excellence in worship is a calling, not a show."},
{q:"Who instructed the Levites about the song, and why was he chosen?", options:["Chenaniah, because he was skilful","Heman, because he was the eldest","Asaph, because he was a seer","David, because he was the king"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:22",verse:"And Chenaniah, chief of the Levites, was for song: he instructed about the song, because he was skilful.", insight:"Chenaniah, because he was skilful; God honors skill, and the skilled should teach."},
{q:"Who blew with the trumpets before the ark of God?", options:["The priests: Shebaniah, Jehoshaphat, Nethaneel, Amasai, Zechariah, Benaiah, and Eliezer","The Levite porters","The elders of Israel","The captains over thousands"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:24",verse:"And Shebaniah, and Jehoshaphat, and Nethaneel, and Amasai, and Zechariah, and Benaiah, and Eliezer, the priests, did blow with the trumpets before the ark of God: and Obed-edom and Jehiah were doorkeepers for the ark.", insight:"The priests with trumpets; every office has its sound in the procession of God."},
{q:"From whose house was the ark brought up with joy?", options:["Out of the house of Obed-edom","Out of the house of Abinadab","Out of the tabernacle at Gibeon","Out of the tent of David"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:25",verse:"So David, and the elders of Israel, and the captains over thousands, went to bring up the ark of the covenant of the LORD out of the house of Obed-edom with joy.", insight:"Out of Obed-edom's house, with joy; what blessed one household now blesses the nation."},
{q:"What sacrifice was offered when God helped the Levites that bare the ark?", options:["Seven bullocks and seven rams","One bullock and one ram","Twelve lambs without blemish","Two turtledoves"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:26",verse:"And it came to pass, when God helped the Levites that bare the ark of the covenant of the LORD, that they offered seven bullocks and seven rams.", insight:"Seven bullocks and seven rams; when God helps, gratitude answers with open hands."},
{q:"What did David wear when the ark was brought up?", options:["A robe of fine linen, and an ephod of linen","The armor of Saul","A crown of pure gold","Sackcloth and ashes"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:27",verse:"And David was clothed with a robe of fine linen, and all the Levites that bare the ark, and the singers, and Chenaniah the master of the song with the singers: David also had upon him an ephod of linen.", insight:"Linen, not armor; the king laid down his glory to celebrate God's."},
{q:"With what sounds did all Israel bring up the ark?", options:["With shouting, and with sound of the cornet, and with trumpets, and with cymbals, psalteries, and harps","With silence and weeping","With the lowing of oxen only","With the beating of war drums"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:28",verse:"Thus all Israel brought up the ark of the covenant of the LORD with shouting, and with sound of the cornet, and with trumpets, and with cymbals, making a noise with psalteries and harps.", insight:"Shouting, trumpets, cymbals, harps; heaven's King deserved earth's loudest welcome."},
{q:"What did Michal the daughter of Saul do when she saw David dancing?", options:["She despised him in her heart","She joined the dancing","She sang with the singers","She wept for joy"], a:0, ref:"1 Chronicles 15:29",verse:"And it came to pass, as the ark of the covenant of the LORD came to the city of David, that Michal the daughter of Saul looking out at a window saw king David dancing and playing: and she despised him in her heart.", insight:"She despised him in her heart; scorn for another's worship reveals a coldness of one's own."}
]}
]);
